{# The shared rules a rendered-Markdown description needs, which are also
   most of what the page needs for the markup it lays out itself.

   They live apart from the rest of `base_styles.jinja` because they have
   two consumers, not one.  A resource page renders `meta.description`
   into a declarative shadow root, and a shadow root is a style boundary:
   `base_styles.jinja` cannot reach inside it, so the description's
   `<style>` includes this file too.  Both sides then read the same text
   -- the shadow root used to carry a hand-copied subset of these rules
   and it fell behind, leaving description tables borderless and
   description headings unstyled (gain#1279).

   What belongs here is decided by the *selector*, not by intent: a rule
   whose selectors name only elements and pseudo-elements belongs here,
   because elements are all that rendered Markdown is made of.  A rule
   naming a class, an id or an attribute stays in `base_styles.jinja` --
   it addresses markup a template emits itself, none of which exists
   inside a shadow root.  Reading the selector is mechanical, so the next
   rule added does not need its author to guess at what counts as
   "content"; it is also what settles `:where(.page-content) img`, which
   names a class and so stays behind with no exception to argue about.

   `body` is the one genuine exception -- an element selector that stays
   in `base_styles.jinja`, because a shadow root has no body element for
   it to match, and the colour it sets reaches the description by
   inheritance regardless.

   Not a second consumer: `about.md` and the annotator doc pages render
   authored Markdown too, but they include `base_styles.jinja` and so
   already receive these rules through it.  Nothing includes both. #}
      *, *::before, *::after {
        box-sizing: border-box;
        font-family: "Roboto", system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
      }

      h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6 {
        color: #5b778c;
      }

      h2 {
        margin-top: 50px;
        margin-bottom: 10px;
      }

      h3,h4 {
        margin-top:0.5em;
        margin-bottom:0.5em;
      }

      table {
        border-collapse: collapse;
        width: 100%
      }

      th {
        background: #ecf1f6;
      }

      td,
      th {
        border: 1px solid #cfd8df;
        padding: 5px 10px;
        overflow-wrap: break-word;
      }

      tr {
        height: 38px;
      }

      ul {
        list-style-type: '-  ';
        padding-left: 15px;
        margin: 0;
      }

      a {
        text-decoration: none;
        color: #24699E;
      }

      a:hover {
        color: #4C93C9;
      }
